---
import SiteLayout from '../../layouts/SiteLayout.astro'
import DocsSidebar from '../../components/DocsSidebar.astro'
---
<SiteLayout title="Custom styling - Open MindMap" description="Theme tokens, runtime classes, and SVG export styling for the Open MindMap v0.9 runtime.">
  <div class="shell docs-layout">
    <DocsSidebar active="styling" />

    <article class="docs-content">
      <span class="eyebrow">Styling guide</span>
      <h1>Make the runtime yours.</h1>
      <p>v0.9 exposes theme modes, a typed token surface, and stable <code>mm-*</code> runtime classes. Use <code>themeTokens</code> for semantic colors and metrics, then use the mounted class names for focused presentation changes.</p>
      <div class="docs-callout">The v0.9 stylesheet entrypoints are separate: import <code>styles/static.css</code>, <code>styles/viewer.css</code>, or <code>styles/editor.css</code> together with any Feature styles you mount.</div>

      <h2 id="custom-styling">Custom styling</h2>
      <p>Choose a mode with <code>theme="light"</code>, <code>theme="dark"</code>, or <code>theme="auto"</code>. Pass a partial <code>themeTokens</code> object when the semantic palette or spacing needs to match the host application.</p>
      <div class="code-block"><pre><code>import &#123; MindMapViewer &#125; from '@xiangfa/mindmap/viewer'
import '@xiangfa/mindmap/styles/viewer.css'

&lt;MindMapViewer
  markdown=&#123;markdown&#125;
  theme="dark"
  themeTokens=&#123;&#123;
    background: '#101621',
    text: '#e9eef8',
    rootFill: '#8f83ff',
    selection: '#55d9ff',
  &#125;&#125;
/&gt;</code></pre></div>

      <h3>Theme mode</h3>
      <p><code>light</code> and <code>dark</code> resolve deterministically. <code>auto</code> follows <code>prefers-color-scheme</code> after hydration; the runtime starts from a light SSR-safe token set and then responds to system changes.</p>

      <h2 id="tokens">Theme tokens</h2>
      <p>The complete token object is shared by the core layout and the mounted runtime. Numeric values are measured in pixels by the layout engine; <code>branches</code> supplies the repeating branch palette.</p>
      <div class="code-block"><pre><code>interface MindMapThemeTokens &#123;
  background: string
  text: string
  mutedText: string
  rootFill: string
  rootText: string
  selection: string
  branches: readonly string[]
  fontFamily: string
  rootFontSize: number
  levelOneFontSize: number
  nodeFontSize: number
  horizontalGap: number
  verticalGap: number
  rootPaddingX: number
  rootPaddingY: number
  nodePaddingX: number
  nodePaddingY: number
&#125;</code></pre></div>
      <div class="docs-table-wrap"><table class="docs-table">
        <thead><tr><th>Group</th><th>Tokens</th><th>Controls</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>Colors</td><td><code>background</code>, <code>text</code>, <code>mutedText</code></td><td>Canvas and regular node text</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Root</td><td><code>rootFill</code>, <code>rootText</code>, <code>rootFontSize</code>, <code>rootPaddingX/Y</code></td><td>Root node shape and label</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Nodes</td><td><code>nodeFontSize</code>, <code>nodePaddingX/Y</code>, <code>levelOneFontSize</code></td><td>Child label hierarchy and boxes</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Edges and focus</td><td><code>branches</code>, <code>selection</code></td><td>Branch colors and selected node outline</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Layout</td><td><code>horizontalGap</code>, <code>verticalGap</code></td><td>Spacing in the projected tree</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Typography</td><td><code>fontFamily</code></td><td>Text measurement and rendering font</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table></div>
      <h3>Default values</h3>
      <div class="docs-table-wrap"><table class="docs-table">
        <thead><tr><th>Token</th><th>Default</th><th>Token</th><th>Default</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td><code>background</code></td><td><code>#ffffff</code></td><td><code>text</code></td><td><code>#253044</code></td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>mutedText</code></td><td><code>#748096</code></td><td><code>rootFill</code></td><td><code>#7367f9</code></td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>rootText</code></td><td><code>#ffffff</code></td><td><code>selection</code></td><td><code>#55d9ff</code></td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>fontFamily</code></td><td><code>Inter, system-ui, sans-serif</code></td><td><code>rootFontSize</code></td><td><code>17</code></td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>levelOneFontSize</code></td><td><code>15</code></td><td><code>nodeFontSize</code></td><td><code>13</code></td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>horizontalGap</code></td><td><code>72</code></td><td><code>verticalGap</code></td><td><code>24</code></td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>rootPaddingX/Y</code></td><td><code>24 / 14</code></td><td><code>nodePaddingX/Y</code></td><td><code>13 / 9</code></td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>branches</code></td><td colspan="3"><code>#7367f9</code>, <code>#1fbca4</code>, <code>#f59e5b</code>, <code>#e76d8c</code>, <code>#4f9cf9</code>, <code>#9a72ee</code>, <code>#68b66b</code>, <code>#e0aa3e</code></td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table></div>

      <h3>CSS variables</h3>
      <p>The shipped token stylesheet exposes the six presentation variables used by mounted surfaces: <code>--mm-background</code>, <code>--mm-text</code>, <code>--mm-muted</code>, <code>--mm-root</code>, <code>--mm-selection</code>, and <code>--mm-font</code>. They are set on each runtime surface from the resolved token object. Prefer <code>themeTokens</code> when a value also affects layout measurement.</p>
      <div class="code-block"><pre><code>/* Presentation-only override for a mounted surface. */
.my-map .mm-node-detail &#123;
  opacity: .68;
&#125;

.my-map .mm-edge &#123;
  stroke-width: 3;
&#125;</code></pre></div>

      <h2 id="classes">Runtime class selectors</h2>
      <p>These classes are available on mounted <code>StaticMindMap</code>, <code>MindMapViewer</code>, and <code>MindMapEditor</code> surfaces. SVG presentation attributes remain the runtime defaults; use a focused selector when a host needs a visual adjustment.</p>
      <div class="docs-table-wrap"><table class="docs-table">
        <thead><tr><th>Class</th><th>Element</th><th>Typical use</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td><code>.mm-static</code>, <code>.mm-static__svg</code></td><td>Static wrapper and SVG</td><td>Size or static surface background</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>.mm-surface</code>, <code>.mm-viewport</code></td><td>Interactive wrapper and viewport SVG</td><td>Surface sizing and focus ring</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>.mm-scene</code>, <code>.mm-edges</code>, <code>.mm-nodes</code></td><td>Scene groups</td><td>Layer-level presentation</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>.mm-edge</code></td><td>Parent-child or cross-link path</td><td>Stroke width, opacity, or dash styling</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>.mm-node</code></td><td>Node group</td><td>Cursor, opacity, or node state styling</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>.mm-node--root</code>, <code>.mm-node--child</code></td><td>Node depth variants</td><td>Differentiate root and child shapes</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>.mm-node-shape</code>, <code>.mm-node-accent</code></td><td>Node background and child accent</td><td>Shape stroke and accent presentation</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>.mm-node-label</code>, <code>.mm-node-detail</code></td><td>Primary and multiline text</td><td>Text selection and opacity</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>.mm-node-selection</code></td><td>Selected root outline</td><td>Selection emphasis</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>.mm-node-tags</code>, <code>.mm-task</code></td><td>Tag and task groups</td><td>Badge or task marker presentation</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>.mm-fold-control</code></td><td>Expand/collapse control</td><td>Control opacity and hover state</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>.mm-inline-content</code></td><td>Formatted foreignObject content</td><td>Inline links, code, math, and image layout</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>.mm-viewport-controls</code></td><td>Viewer/editor zoom controls</td><td>Position and control chrome</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>.mm-editor-toolbar</code>, <code>.mm-context-menu</code></td><td>Editor chrome</td><td>Toolbar or context menu layout</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table></div>

      <h3>Branch colors</h3>
      <p>Branch colors are resolved from <code>themeTokens.branches</code> and cycle by branch index. This is the supported way to set per-branch colors because branch indices are layout data rather than public DOM attributes.</p>
      <div class="code-block"><pre><code>&lt;MindMapViewer
  markdown=&#123;markdown&#125;
  themeTokens=&#123;&#123;
    branches: ['#ff7f9f', '#55d9ff', '#72e4b8', '#ffc36a'],
  &#125;&#125;
/&gt;</code></pre></div>

      <h2 id="export-styling">SVG and PNG export</h2>
      <p><code>renderMindMapToSvg</code> produces standalone SVG with resolved colors, an accessible title and description, and escaped user content. The Editor export Feature can prepare SVG or rasterize it to PNG. Exported files do not depend on the page's CSS variables, so set semantic values through the <code>theme</code> and <code>themeTokens</code> options passed to the export path.</p>
      <div class="code-block"><pre><code>import &#123; prepareMindMapSvg &#125; from '@xiangfa/mindmap/features/export'

const svg = await prepareMindMapSvg(document, &#123;
  extensions,
  theme: &#123; background: '#101621', text: '#e9eef8' &#125;,
  title: 'Product strategy',
  description: 'A rendered product strategy map',
&#125;)</code></pre></div>
      <p>Remote HTTP(S) images are denied by default. Authorize intended browser origins with <code>remoteImagePolicy</code>. Before PNG export, embed remote images through an explicitly authorized host <code>imageResolver</code>; the resolver may return only a safe PNG, JPEG, GIF, or WebP data URL. Unresolved remote URLs remain subject to the policy, and raw SVG input is capped at 16 MiB before rasterization. Math rendering uses the optional KaTeX peer when the LaTeX extension is active.</p>

      <h2 id="style-entries">Style entrypoints</h2>
      <div class="api-grid">
        <div class="api-card"><strong><code>@xiangfa/mindmap/styles/tokens.css</code></strong><p>Shared token variables for mounted surfaces.</p></div>
        <div class="api-card"><strong><code>@xiangfa/mindmap/styles/static.css</code></strong><p>Static SVG wrapper and scene presentation.</p></div>
        <div class="api-card"><strong><code>@xiangfa/mindmap/styles/viewer.css</code></strong><p>Viewer viewport, focus, controls, and semantic tree.</p></div>
        <div class="api-card"><strong><code>@xiangfa/mindmap/styles/editor.css</code></strong><p>Editor toolbar, editing controls, and context menu.</p></div>
      </div>
      <p>Feature styles are separate imports such as <code>styles/features/ai.css</code> and <code>styles/features/search.css</code>. This keeps unused editor chrome out of static and viewer surfaces.</p>
    </article>

